IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sumlma-statement-days`

-- Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Act 1999 ss 15A, 20B with the Commissioner's two instruments -- worked
-- cases, from the member's seat.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited texts (the Act; F2009L04037; F2009L01210), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario life
-- raised this; the facts are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL throughout.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 15A days. Ron's money became unclaimed money on 15 March 2027: the next unclaimed money day is 30 June 2027, whose
-- scheduled statement day is 31 October 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `my money is unclaimed money (s 17(1))` (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 31 10 2027)
-- Qualifying on 30 June 2027 itself: reported "as at the end of" that day: 31 October 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `my money is unclaimed money (s 17(1))` (Date 30 6 2027) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 31 10 2027)
-- Qualifying on 1 July 2027: the 31 December 2027 unclaimed money day, paid by 30 April 2028.
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `my money is unclaimed money (s 17(1))` (Date 1 7 2027) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 30 4 2028)
-- Mia's account became a lost member account on 10 December 2026: 31 December 2026, so 30 April 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `my account is a lost member account (s 24E(1))` (Date 10 12 2026) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 30 4 2027)
-- An inactive low-balance account from 1 February 2027: 30 June 2027, so 31 October 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `my account is an inactive low-balance account (s 20QD(1))` (Date 1 2 2027) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 31 10 2027)
-- Before the 2009 instrument was registered: not covered.
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `my money is unclaimed money (s 17(1))` (Date 1 6 2009) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `not covered: my money qualified before 28 October 2009, when the unclaimed money days now in force were registered, and the earlier days are not deposited`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 20B days and s 20F(1). Lena: notice given 15 April 2027. The next Part 3A scheduled statement day is 30 April 2027, less
-- than 28 days away, so the following one: 31 October 2027 (s 20F(1)(b)). The Regulations identify no later day ((c)).
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `the Commissioner has given my fund a notice that I am a former temporary resident (s 20C)` (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 31 10 2027)
-- Notice on 1 April 2027: 29 days before 30 April: 30 April 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `the Commissioner has given my fund a notice that I am a former temporary resident (s 20C)` (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 30 4 2027)
-- Notice on 2 April 2027: exactly 28 days before, not less: 30 April 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `the Commissioner has given my fund a notice that I am a former temporary resident (s 20C)` (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 2 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 30 4 2027)
-- Notice on 30 April 2027 itself: the next day after it is 31 October 2027, more than 28 days away: 31 October 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `the Commissioner has given my fund a notice that I am a former temporary resident (s 20C)` (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 30 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 31 10 2027)
-- Notice on 30 October 2027: 31 October is 1 day away, so 30 April 2028. On 1 November 2027: 30 April 2028.
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `the Commissioner has given my fund a notice that I am a former temporary resident (s 20C)` (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 30 10 2027) FALSE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 30 4 2028)
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `the Commissioner has given my fund a notice that I am a former temporary resident (s 20C)` (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 11 2027) FALSE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 30 4 2028)
-- Notice on 1 May 2009, before the first Part 3A day (15 June 2009): 45 days before it, so 15 June 2009.
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `the Commissioner has given my fund a notice that I am a former temporary resident (s 20C)` (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 5 2009) FALSE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 15 6 2009)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The Act's own days, unchanged: an ERF low balance account, 30 June 2021; a voluntary payment, no day.
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `my account is in an eligible rollover fund (s 21C)` (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE EQUALS `by the end of the day` (Date 30 6 2021)
#ASSERT `By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` `my fund chooses to pay because it believes it is in my best interests (s 22)` (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `no day: my fund may pay the Commissioner under s 22 but is not required to`
